<title>SPAIN: Seat posts 1996 profit of 5.34 bln ptas.</title>
<headline>Seat posts 1996 profit of 5.34 bln ptas.</headline>
<dateline>BARCELONA 1997-03-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Volkswagen's Spanish unit Seat posted net profit of 5.34 billion pesetas in 1996 versus a loss of 11.29 billion pesetas in 1995, the company said on Tuesday.  </p>
<p>Other figures were given as follow (in billions of pesetas versus 1995, unless stated):</p>
<p> Sales (units)		  426,324  vs  341,152</p>
<p> Production (units)	   415,213  vs  343,444</p>
<p> Sales			    607.31   vs  456.52</p>
<p> Net profit/loss		  5.34   vs  (11.29)</p>
<p> Amortisation		    44.80   vs   54.82</p>
<p> Investment			31.87   vs   22.51</p>
<p>Seat attributed the 1996 turnaround to increased income from sales, improved productivity, cost reductions and asset sales.</p>
<p>Seat said sales income in the two months to February rose 32.5 percent to 114.84 bilion pesetas.</p>
<p>-- Robert Hetz, Madrid newsroom +341 585 2160</p>
</text>
